# GenmojiTalk Privacy Policy

**Effective Date**: May 22, 2026  
**Last Updated**: May 22, 2026  
**Developer**: Guan PeiHao (Individual)  
**Contact**: artyomguan@gmail.com

---

## 1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how the **GenmojiTalk** mobile application
("the App") handles your information. This document applies globally
to all users of the App. By using the App you agree to this policy.

**Short version: we do not collect, transmit, or sell any personal
information. Everything you create stays on your device unless you
explicitly choose to share it.**

## 2. Information We Do NOT Collect

We do not collect, store on remote servers, or transmit any of the
following:

- Your name, email address, phone number, or other contact details
- Your device identifiers (IDFA, UUID, advertising ID)
- Your location
- Your contacts, calendar, or messages
- Analytics events, crash logs, usage statistics
- Any data you create within the App (custom emoji names, voice
  recordings, Genmoji, collections, chains)

We do not use any third-party analytics SDKs, ad networks, or
tracking frameworks.

## 3. Data Stored Locally on Your Device

The App stores the following data exclusively in your device's local
sandbox (Application Support / Documents) and / or the iOS App
Group container:

| Data | Stored Where | When Deleted |
|------|--------------|--------------|
| Custom emoji names (My Dictionary) | SwiftData local DB | App uninstall |
| Voice recordings (UserVoiceClip) | Local audio files | App uninstall |
| Genmoji you create | SwiftData + PNG file | App uninstall |
| Voice It video drafts | App Support directory | App uninstall |
| Voice Tag-Team chain manifests | Embedded in exported MP4 metadata | When user deletes draft |
| Collections and segments | SwiftData + media files | App uninstall |
| Settings preferences | UserDefaults | App uninstall |
| Subscription / purchase state | Apple StoreKit (managed by Apple) | Tied to your Apple ID |

You can delete all App data at any time by uninstalling the App.

## 4. iCloud Sync (Future Feature)

A future version of the App may offer optional iCloud Sync so your
dictionary, recordings, and collections are available across your
Apple devices. When iCloud Sync is enabled:

- Data is end-to-end encrypted by Apple's iCloud service.
- Data is stored in your personal iCloud account, not on our servers.
- We never have access to your iCloud data.
- You can disable sync at any time in the App's Settings or in iOS
  Settings → Apple ID → iCloud.

## 5. Permissions We Request

The App may request the following iOS permissions, all of which are
optional and used solely for the features described:

- **Microphone**: to record voice clips for your personal dictionary
  (only when you tap a Record button)
- **Photo Library** (read-only via PhotosPicker): to import images,
  GIFs, Live Photos and videos for the Voice It feature (you select
  individual items; the App never accesses your full library)
- **Files / iCloud Drive** (via DocumentPicker): to import shared
  Voice It chain videos

We do not request: location, contacts, calendars, health data, motion
data, camera, or any other permissions.

## 6. Apple System Services

The App uses the following on-device Apple system services. Data
handled by these services is governed by Apple's Privacy Policy
([apple.com/privacy](https://www.apple.com/privacy/)):

- **AVSpeechSynthesizer** (Text-to-Speech): used to read out your
  custom phrases. Runs entirely on-device.
- **Personal Voice** (iOS 17+, optional): if you have created a
  Personal Voice in iOS Settings, the App can use it for in-app
  playback. The Personal Voice model stays on your device.
- **Apple Intelligence Genmoji** (iOS 18+, optional): when you create
  a Genmoji via the system keyboard, generation may happen on-device
  or via Apple's Private Cloud Compute. The resulting glyph PNG is
  saved locally in the App's sandbox.

The App does not send any of this data to our servers.

## 7. In-App Purchases

Subscription and one-time purchases are processed by Apple's
StoreKit framework. Apple receives your payment information; we do
not. We only receive confirmation that a purchase is valid.
Subscriptions and the Lifetime purchase support **Family Sharing**.

## 8. Children's Privacy

The App is rated 4+ on the App Store. The App does not knowingly
collect any personal information from children or anyone of any
other age, because **we do not collect personal information at all**.

## 9. Your Rights

Because we do not collect or store your personal information on our
servers, there is no remote data to access, correct, port, or delete.
You have full control:

- **Access**: all data is on your device, accessible through the App's
  UI (My Dictionary, Voice It Recents, etc.)
- **Delete**: uninstall the App to remove all local data
- **Export**: use the Voice It Share feature to export your creations

If you have questions, contact us at: **artyomguan@gmail.com**

## 10. Regional Notes

- **EEA users (GDPR)**: we do not act as a data controller because
  we do not collect personal data. Apple is the processor for any
  payment and Apple system service data.
- **California users (CCPA)**: we do not sell or share your personal
  information for any purpose.
- **Mainland China users (PIPL / 个人信息保护法)**: 我们不收集您的
  个人信息，所有数据存储在您的本地设备上，不传输至任何境外服务器
  （iCloud 同步若启用，由 Apple 加密处理并存储于您本人的 iCloud
  账户）。详见下方中文版本。

## 11. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes
will be highlighted with an updated "Last Updated" date at the top
of this document. Continued use of the App after changes constitutes
acceptance of the updated policy.

## 12. Contact

For any privacy-related question or request, please email:
**artyomguan@gmail.com**

